      "suites": ["test_sun"],
      "expect": "caught"
    },
    {
      "name": "the date is 1.7 ms out, the size of TDB - TT",
      "file": "src/astro/Sun.cpp",
      "find": "eraEpv00(date.day, date.fraction, heliocentric, barycentric)",
      "replace": "eraEpv00(date.day, date.fraction - (0.0017 / 86400.0), heliocentric, barycentric)",
      "suites": ["test_sun"],
      "expect": "caught",
      "why": "Caught by the span cases alone, never by the accuracy budget: 1.7 ms of solar motion is 7e-5 arcsec against a 0.02 arcsec claim, and the shifted date crosses ERFA's boundary at the edge epochs. This mutant confirms what astro/Sun.hpp says the suite cannot see rather than contradicting it, and is kept for exactly that reason."
    },
    {
